EXAMPLE a key is a property named by its key, or by AS, documented, or PARTIAL; FN is a parameterized accessor
  SOURCE CATALOG UiCopy IN polski.presentation
  SOURCE   KEY save
  SOURCE   KEY close AS CloseButton DOC "Closes the current dialog."
  SOURCE   KEY missions PARTIAL
  SOURCE   FN languageName "lang.$code" code
  SOURCE END
  EXPECT rendered.kt val Save: String get() = text("save")
  EXPECT rendered.kt val CloseButton: String get() = text("close")
  EXPECT rendered.kt /** Closes the current dialog. */
  EXPECT rendered.kt val Missions: String get() = text("missions")
  EXPECT rendered.kt fun languageName(code: String): String = text("lang.$code")
  EXPECT unrendered.kt val Close:

EXAMPLE a key twice is refused at the second
  SOURCE CATALOG UiCopy IN polski.presentation
  SOURCE   KEY save
  SOURCE   KEY save
  SOURCE END
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_DUPLICATE at 3:7

EXAMPLE a catalog without IN fails
  SOURCE CATALOG UiCopy
  SOURCE   KEY save
  SOURCE END
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_SYNTAX at 1:9
